                <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</owl:hasValue>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en"> is the SI unit of magnetic field strength. One ampere per meter is equal to π/250 oersteds (12.566  371 millioersteds) in CGS units. The ampere per meter is also the SI unit of &quot;magnetization&quot; in the sense of magnetic dipole moment per unit volume; in this context 1 A/m = 0.001 emu per cubic centimeter.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/coherentsiunits#"/>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
