        <ns1:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>A/m</ns1:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en"> is the SI unit of magnetic field strength. One ampere per meter is equal to π/250 oersteds (12.566  371 millioersteds) in CGS units. The ampere per meter is also the SI unit of &quot;magnetization&quot; in the sense of magnetic dipole moment per unit volume; in this context 1 A/m = 0.001 emu per cubic centimeter.

-- QUDT</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
