        <ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>m3.s-1</ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
        <ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>m3/s</ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
        <ns1:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>m³/s</ns1:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A cubic metre per second (m³s⁻¹, m³/s), cumecs or cubic meter per second in American English) is a derived SI unit of flow rate equal to that of a stere or cube with sides of one metre ( u0303 39.37 in) in length exchanged or moving each second. It is popularly used for water flow, especially in rivers and streams, and fractions for HVAC values measuring air flow.

-- QUDT</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
