        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">OneManifold</skos:prefLabel>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A topological space with the property that each point has a neighborhood that is homeomorphic to an open subset of 1-dimensional Euclidean space.</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
        <ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">One-dimensional manifolds include lines and circles, but not self-crossing curves. Two-dimensional manifolds are also called surfaces. Examples include the plane, the sphere, and the torus, and also the Klein bottle and real projective plane.</ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    </owl:Class>
