        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A &apos;Semiosis&apos; that involves an &apos;Observer&apos; that perceives another &apos;Physical&apos; (the &apos;Object&apos;) through a specific perception mechanism and produces a &apos;Property&apos; (the &apos;Sign&apos;) that stands for the result of that particular perception according to a well defined conventional procedure.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry/modules/electrochemistry-testing#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Determination</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Characterisation</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:example xml:lang="en">Assigning the word &quot;red&quot; as sign for an object provides an information to all other interpreters about the outcome of a specific observation procedure according to the determiner.</skos:example>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Determination</skos:prefLabel>
        <ns1:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db>EquivalentTo: Estimation or Observation</ns1:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db>
