        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A programming language entity expressing a formal detailed plan of what a software is intended to do.</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
        <ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A source code is the companion of an application, being it the entity used to generate the application list of CPU executable instructions.</ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
        <ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">Source code (also referred to as source or code) is the version of software as it is originally written (i.e., typed into a computer) by a human in plain text (i.e., human readable alphanumeric characters).</ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
