        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">For an atom or nucleus, this energy is quantized and can be written as:

    W = g μ M B

where g is the appropriate g factor, μ is mostly the Bohr magneton or nuclear magneton, M is magnetic quantum number, and B is magnitude of the magnetic flux density.

-- ISO 80000</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Vector quantity μ causing a change to its energy ΔW in an external magnetic field of field flux density B:

    ΔW = −μ · B</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/isq#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MagneticDipoleMoment</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">MagneticDipoleMoment</skos:prefLabel>
