        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Categorisation of intentional agencies by their kind.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/reference/agency#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">IntentionalAgencyByKind</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">IntentionalAgencyByKind</skos:prefLabel>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">Categorisation of intentional agencies by their kind.</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8b0923ab_b500_477b_9ce9_8b3a3e4dc4f2 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8b0923ab_b500_477b_9ce9_8b3a3e4dc4f2">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_bc37743c_37c4_4ec7_9d58_d1aae5567352"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A state that is a collection of sufficiently large number of other parts such that:
- it is the bearer of qualities that can exists only by the fact that it is a sum of parts
- the smallest partition dV of the state volume in which we are interested in, contains enough parts to be statistically consistent: n [#/m3] x dV [m3] &gt;&gt; 1</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/reference/electrochemistry-reference#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ContinuumSubstance</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ContinuumSubstance</skos:prefLabel>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A state that is a collection of sufficiently large number of other parts such that:
- it is the bearer of qualities that can exists only by the fact that it is a sum of parts
- the smallest partition dV of the state volume in which we are interested in, contains enough parts to be statistically consistent: n [#/m3] x dV [m3] &gt;&gt; 1</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
        <ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A continuum is made of a sufficient number of parts that it continues to exists as continuum individual even after the loss of one of them i.e. a continuum is a redundant.</ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
        <ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A continuum is not necessarily small (i.e. composed by the minimum amount of sates to fulfill the definition).

A single continuum individual can be the whole fluid in a pipe.</ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
        <ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A continuum is the bearer of properties that are generated by the interactions of parts such as viscosity and thermal or electrical conductivity.</ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8b1367d6_0133_4b56_acc1_fa8b058169e3 -->

