        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A common metric unit of length or distance. One kilometer equals exactly 1000 meters, about 0.621 371 19 mile, 1093.6133 yards, or 3280.8399 feet. Oddly, higher multiples of the meter are rarely used; even the distances to the farthest galaxies are usually measured in kilometers.

-- QUDT</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
