            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The kilogram, symbol kg, is the SI unit of mass. It is defined by taking the fixed numerical value of the Planck constant h to be 6.62607015×10−34 when expressed in the unit J s, which is equal to kg m2 s−1, where the metre and the second are defined in terms of c and ∆νCs.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siunits#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Kilogram</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Kilogram</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Kilogram</skos:prefLabel>
        <schema:unitCode>KGM</schema:unitCode>
        <ns1:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM</ns1:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
        <ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>kg</ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
        <ns1:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kilogram</ns1:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25>
        <ns1:EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84 xml:lang="en">The kilogram, symbol kg, is the SI unit of mass. It is defined by taking the fixed numerical value of the Planck constant h to be 6.62607015×10−34 when expressed in the unit J s, which is equal to kg m2 s−1, where the metre and the second are defined in terms of c and ∆νCs.</ns1:EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84>
        <ns1:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kilogram?oldid=493633626</ns1:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
