                <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</owl:hasValue>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The &quot;microfarad&quot; (symbolized μ F) is a unit of capacitance, equivalent to 0.000001 (10 to the -6th power) farad. The microfarad is a moderate unit of capacitance. In utility alternating-current (AC) and audio-frequency (AF) circuits, capacitors with values on the order of 1 μ F or more are common. At radio frequencies (RF), a smaller unit, the picofarad (pF), is often used.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
