        <ns1:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroFARAD</ns1:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
        <ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>uF</ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
        <ns1:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>µF</ns1:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">The &quot;microfarad&quot; (symbolized μ F) is a unit of capacitance, equivalent to 0.000001 (10 to the -6th power) farad. The microfarad is a moderate unit of capacitance. In utility alternating-current (AC) and audio-frequency (AF) circuits, capacitors with values on the order of 1 μ F or more are common. At radio frequencies (RF), a smaller unit, the picofarad (pF), is often used.

-- QUDT</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    </owl:Class>
    


