        <ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>W.m-2</ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
        <ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>W/m2</ns1:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
        <ns1:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>W/m²</ns1:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">&quot;Watt per Square Meter} is a unit of irradiance defined as the power received per area. This is a unit in the category of Energy flux. It is also known as watts per square meter, watt per square metre, watts per square metre, watt/square meter, watt/square metre. This unit is commonly used in the SI unit system. Watt Per Square Meter (W/m²) has a dimension of MT^{-3&quot; where M is mass, and T is time. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.

-- QUDT</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
