        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This is the thermodynamic electromotive force of the cell. The measured open-circuit voltage approaches it as the cell relaxes, but need not reach it, for example when an electrode rests on a hysteresis branch.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">open-circuit voltage of a cell when all interfacial charge-transfer equilibria are established; equal to minus the reaction Gibbs energy divided by the charge number and the Faraday constant, and to the difference of the equilibrium electrode potentials of the two electrodes</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry/reference/electrochemistry-quantities#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EquilibriumCellVoltage</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ElectromotiveForce</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">EquilibriumCellPotential</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ReversibleCellVoltage</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">EquilibriumCellVoltage</skos:prefLabel>
