        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The kinetic current is partially or entirely controlled by the rate of the chemical reaction. This reaction may be heterogeneous, occurring at an electrode-solution interface (surface reaction), or it may be homo- geneous, occurring at some distance from the interface (bulk reaction).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">faradaic current of an electroactive substance B formed by a prior chemical reaction from another substance Y that is no electroactive at the potential at which B is electrochemically transformed</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry/reference/electrochemistry-quantities#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">KineticCurrent</rdfs:label>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">KineticCurrent</skos:prefLabel>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">faradaic current of an electroactive substance B formed by a prior chemical reaction from another substance Y that is no electroactive at the potential at which B is electrochemically transformed</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
        <ns1:EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2 xml:lang="en">https://goldbook.iupac.org/terms/view/K03399</ns1:EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2>
    </owl:Class>
