        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Deprecated in 0.38.0: the electrode polarity and the bearing component belong to the cell structure (hasNegativeElectrode / hasPositiveElectrode, hasCoating, hasActiveMaterial), not to the class name. The class is kept, with a defining axiom, so that data typed with it still classifies and data stated through the structure classifies under it.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">activation energy of the rate constant of the negative electrode reaction</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry/reference/electrochemistry-quantities#"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NegativeElectrodeActivationEnergyOfReaction</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">NegativeElectrodeActivationEnergyOfReaction</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">State the polarity through the cell structure instead: the cell hasNegativeElectrode an electrode, an ElectrodeReaction hasParticipant that electrode, the reaction hasProperty a ReactionRateConstant, and the rate constant hasProperty an ActivationEnergy.</skos:scopeNote>
        <ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">activation energy of the rate constant of the negative electrode reaction</ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
        <electrochemistry_0a5b99ee_995b_4899_a79b_925a4086da37 xml:lang="en">[&apos;Parameterisation&apos;,&apos;Negative electrode&apos;,&apos;Reaction rate constant activation energy [J.mol-1]&apos;]</electrochemistry_0a5b99ee_995b_4899_a79b_925a4086da37>
    </owl:Class>
    


